  PART 6: SELF-CONJUGATE RSK AND THE DURFEE SQUARE
========================================================================

  From Part 1: RSK shapes of tournaments are (mostly) self-conjugate.
  A self-conjugate partition has a DURFEE SQUARE of side d,
  where d = max{i : lambda_i >= i}.

  Self-conjugate partitions correspond to SYMMETRIC representations.
  For tournaments: the RSK self-conjugacy means the P-tableau
  has a symmetric structure.

